  "description": "Red Hat Satellite 6.17.13 update addresses multiple critical security vulnerabilities affecting components such as Puma, PyJWT, ansible-core, candlepin, foreman, pulpcore, and others. These vulnerabilities include HTTP request smuggling, authentication bypass, remote code execution, broken authorization, denial of service, cross-tenant data disclosure, arbitrary file read, token forgery, and cryptographic integrity compromise. The update also includes various bug fixes to improve system stability and functionality.",
